+# PQBRAK-off Beerten nose regression (2026-09-11)
+
+`t_pqbrak_off_batch5` checks the global default-off option, saved-option
+upgrade, native-load cache restoration, unchanged equivalent demands,
+low-voltage ordinary PF agreement, and the full automatic Beerten NOSE run
+at the original, half, and quarter CPF step sizes. It checks full equations,
+constant-load schedules, and returned voltage tables at every accepted point,
+including the localized nose. See `docs/PQBRAK_MODEL_POLICY.md`.
+
+The historical `t_mpxt_psse` suite explicitly opts into PQBRAK; its prior
+modeling assertions are preserved. Prior output directories remain evidence
+of their original scenario and are not rewritten when defaults change.
